"""
Data Appreciation — what every computer user should know about data, from the very basics to intermediate
(owner, 7 Nov 2026: "The Data Appreciation was supposed be the very basics to intermediate of what every computer
user should [know]").

The arc, in the order a person actually meets it: data on a computer and how it is measured; files, folders and
names; saving and backing up; the keyboard and entering data accurately; the spreadsheet, then formulas; sorting,
filtering and tidy tables; summaries and charts; finding and checking information online; staying safe (passwords,
2-step verification, phishing, personal data); sharing, file types and working together; and a project that uses
every one of them again. Free tools only — any computer's own file manager, Google Sheets (or LibreOffice Calc),
Google Forms — and nothing a phone cannot also do.
"""
from lessons import SHEETS_FN, KHAN_STATS, NDPC, OWID

